{
  "recipe_version": 1,
  "name": "Carbon network from six linkers",
  "description": "Benzene rings (C6), acetylene (C2), trigonal sp2 carbon nodes, allene (a C3 cumulene), cyclopropenyl nodes (a C3 ring) and propargyl linkers (-CH2-C#C-), each able to join itself and the others, except where GAFF would give the wrong bond: an alkyne's cg end to another's ch end (the triple bond's length), cyclopropenyl to cyclopropenyl and allene to cyclopropenyl (double-bond lengths). GAFF 1.81 parameters (params/gaff_carbon), a rigid-body optimisation with dihedrals after each pass, then Poreblazer. See docs/carbon-linkers.md.",
  "cell": {
    "box": [
      30,
      30,
      30
    ],
    "bond_margin": 0.5,
    "bond_angle_margin": 15,
    "typed_bond_lengths": true
  },
